EGPL Bot Privacy Policy
Last updated: October 4, 2026

EGPL Bot uses Google OAuth to access Google Drive. It may read, create, update, and organize files within Google Drive as necessary to maintain the EGPL archive.
The application does not use Google Drive data for advertising, profiling, or unrelated purposes.

How data is used
Google Drive access is used only to:
- store and update EGPL Discord archive files;
- read existing archive files when necessary for synchronization or recovery;
- preserve archive history and file organization;
- maintain automated archive updates;
- analyze archived EGPL Discord activity for the retrospective XP Leveling project,  a one-time event after the retrospective XP assigning is complete.

Data sharing
EGPL Bot does not sell Google user data.
Google user data is not shared with advertisers or used for advertising purposes.

Data retention
Archive files remain in the authorized Google Drive account until they are manually deleted or otherwise removed by the account owner.
Authentication credentials are used only to allow the automated archive system to access the authorized Google Drive account.
Revoking access
Access to Google Drive can be revoked at any time through the Google Account permissions/security settings.
Revoking access will prevent EGPL Bot from performing future automatic updates of the EGPL Archives until authorization is restored.
